{"parentUuid":"da1f518f-2bb4-4f6c-8c06-65a7b48b2e77","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"eed3b582-9d5c-4660-93a0-d07811f6212c","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"rustling-honking-llama","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01XDG62c63vDPBi9h4rfAKmo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my thorough search, I can see that the `simpo_loss` function in the SimPO trainer is incomplete (it just has a stub that returns undefined variables). Let me now provide you with a comprehensive summary of what I found regarding DPO/CPO loss implementations with sigmoid and hinge loss types.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI've searched the /root/SimPO repository and related Python files for implementations of DPO/CPO loss with sigmoid and hinge loss types. Here's what I found:\n\n### Configuration Files\n\n**File: `/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py` (Lines 28-59)**\n\n```python\nlabel_smoothing (`float`, defaults to 0):\n    The label smoothing factor. This argument is required if you want to use the default data collator.\nloss_type (`str`, defaults to `sigmoid`):\n    The type of loss to use. This argument is required if you want to use the default data collator.\n\n...\n\nlabel_smoothing: float = 0\nloss_type: Literal[\"sigmoid\", \"hinge\"] = \"sigmoid\"\n```\n\nThis shows the configuration supports both `sigmoid` and `hinge` loss types with a `label_smoothing` parameter.\n\n### Loss Function Handling\n\n**File: `/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py` (Lines 253-262)**\n\n```python\n# if args.loss_type in [\"hinge\"] and args.label_smoothing > 0:\n#     warnings.warn(\n#         \"You are using a loss type that does not support label smoothing. Ignoring label_smoothing parameter.\"\n#     )\n\nself.beta = args.beta\nself.gamma_beta_ratio = args.gamma_beta_ratio\nself.sft_weight = args.sft_weight\nself.label_smoothing = args.label_smoothing\nself.loss_type = args.loss_type\n```\